"counts": {"high": 1, "mid": 15, "low": 2}, "transcripts": [{"start": "00:14:22", "end": "00:15:37", "text": "I am feeling like putting a spotlight on vocalists. Anytime I talk about this music, I'm always talking about how important vocalists have been in pushing the sound and into making it kind of what it is today, obviously. the sound does rely a lot on beat and we know this we know heavy instrumentals heavy bass heavy log drum all of those things big characteristics of the sound but there are so many vocalists that have brought people into the sound that have sort of paved the way for the new style of piano that I think we're in at the moment and on the way to the station I was actually listening to a couple the older songs I was like why did these songs ever kind of disappear and I thought why not spread the love and show what the evolution of the sound has been really so that's kind of the bag that I'm feeling like jumping into today but if there are any of your favorite vocalists or anything that you want to share with me send me a text on 0435 123 945 we've got the whole hour together. Stay tuned."}, {"start": "00:41:09", "end": "00:43:34", "text": "You are tuned into The Yanos Show on FBi Radio 94.5 and somehow we're left with 20 minutes left of this week's show. It happens every time I get so caught up in everything that I'm playing that I'm like, oh, there's not that much left of this week's show. But I hope you've been enjoying it as much as I have been and playing a lot of the tracks that I did play. a lot of them are a lot older a couple years i would say but all of them had such to me at least an important role in just the evolution of the sound from not just the producers but how important again the vocalists are in just tying the whole song together the memorable sort of melodies lyrics all of that stuff um that kind of keeps people coming back to this type of music and And I just find it so interesting how the sound has kind of evolved and how vocals in this sound have evolved as well. If anyone kind of keeps up with new music and all of that, you would notice that it's a lot more instrumental focused. We've got a lot more MCs that are taking over in the vocalist space. so you'll see a lot of the chants that you hear when you go out being said over the music is actually being integrated into the actual songs now and I find that interesting as well and it's just interesting to see sort of how again that evolution has come into play I think it's so intriguing to kind of have been there from the start to where I think vocals were placed so much higher above even what the instrumental was like to kind of seeing where we're at now it's a lot more sound a lot more percussion i want to say and if you agree with me send me a text on 0435 123 945 might play some new stuff i think that's where i've kind of landed at the moment this song is off of the new tycoon album i say listen to that that was a great album he's a great producer again one of those ones that's a bit more under the radar but with all of that being said there are a couple announcements that I have to make just before the show ends for this week so please do stay tuned we've got about 15 minutes left"}, {"start": "00:57:35", "end": "01:00:00", "text": "You are tuning into The Anna Show on FBi Radio 94.5 and I had a couple announcements I wanted to make in terms of what's going on in the scene in the next couple of weeks and the first thing I will say is next Saturday, oh my goodness it's such a big day, next Saturday Durban Gogol is coming to Australia. for those of you who don't know who that is she is probably one of the biggest exports out of South Africa at the moment well not even at the moment in the entire scene I would say um she's got so many big hits she is a great producer vocalist as well so many good vocals you wouldn't even pick up that it's her singing she's so amazing but she is gracing Australia I think she's already here actually she did a show in canberra last night she's playing in perth today and then next week will be sydney brisbane i want to say i think brisbane's this week and melbourne um i don't think there's anyone that's more excited than me personally um i would say i'm a nonchalant person but until now i can't be anymore and i'm so excited to be a part of the lineup a part of even just people that get to watch her play in real life the last time she came was 2024 for promised land and that was so amazing in itself to just have a show dedicated to her so amazing the box is bringing her out for the sydney show and i am so excited to be there probably see me squealing fangirling in the corner on the actual night but the lineup does include myself and a couple of other sydney favorites a couple of my friends on this lineup and i'm so excited to be a part of that but do grab your tickets do get involved i think she is one not to miss personally not just because she's my fave but with that being said if you are free tonight i will also be playing at the box as well i think that's at arcade this evening from about 10 onwards so hopefully i see you there catch me on at midnight for that as well but thank you all for tuning in for this week's show i will be back same time same place for all the same vibes"}], "fbi_json": [{"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:00:00"}, "track": {"title": "Minutes of Pure Joy", "artists": [{"name": "Bitumen"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:02:00"}, "track": {"title": "Ngimephi Nawe", "artists": [{"name": "MOREKI & Smanga"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:06:00"}, "track": {"title": "Ngisokola (feat. Eemoh, Daliwonga & Xduppy)", "artists": [{"name": "ShaunMusiQ & Ftears"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:09:00"}, "track": {"title": "Montana", "artists": [{"name"